msgid ""
"There are situations where you might want to build software from source "
"files that are external to and thus outside of the OpenEmbedded build "
"system. For example, suppose you have a project that includes a new BSP "
"with a heavily customized kernel. And, you want to minimize exposing the "
"build system to the development team so that they can focus on their "
"project and maintain everyone's workflow as much as possible. In this "
"case, you want a kernel source directory on the development machine where"
" the development occurs. You want the recipe's :term:`SRC_URI` variable "
"to point to the external directory and use it as is, not copy it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../dev-manual/building.rst:708
msgid ""
"To build from software that comes from an external source, all you need "
"to do is inherit the :ref:`ref-classes-externalsrc` class and then set "
"the :term:`EXTERNALSRC` variable to point to your external source code. "
"Here are the statements to put in your :ref:`structure-build-conf-"
"local.conf` file::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../dev-manual/building.rst:716
msgid ""
"This next example shows how to accomplish the same thing by setting "
":term:`EXTERNALSRC` in the recipe itself or in the recipe's append file::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../dev-manual/building.rst:724
msgid ""
"In order for these settings to take effect, you must globally or locally "
"inherit the :ref:`ref-classes-externalsrc` class."
msgstr ""

#: ../../dev-manual/building.rst:727
msgid ""
"By default, :ref:`ref-classes-externalsrc` builds the source code in a "
"directory separate from the external source directory as specified by "
":term:`EXTERNALSRC`. If you need to have the source built in the same "
"directory in which it resides, or some other nominated directory, you can"
" set :term:`EXTERNALSRC_BUILD` to point to that directory::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../dev-manual/building.rst:739
msgid ""
"The values of :term:`EXTERNALSRC` and :term:`EXTERNALSRC_BUILD` must be "
"absolute paths."
msgstr ""

#: ../../dev-manual/building.rst:743
msgid "Replicating a Build Offline"
msgstr ""

#: ../../dev-manual/building.rst:745
msgid ""
"It can be useful to take a \"snapshot\" of upstream sources used in a "
"build and then use that \"snapshot\" later to replicate the build "
"offline. To do so, you need to first prepare and populate your downloads "
"directory with your \"snapshot\" of files. Once your downloads directory "
"is ready, you can use it at any time and from any machine to replicate "
"your build."
