#: ../../dev-manual/development-shell.rst:4
msgid "Using a Development Shell"
msgstr ""

#: ../../dev-manual/development-shell.rst:6
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"When debugging certain commands or even when just editing packages, "
"``devshell`` can be a useful tool. When you invoke ``devshell``, all "
"tasks up to and including :ref:`ref-tasks-patch` are run for the "
"specified target. Then, a new terminal is opened and you are placed in "
"``${``\\ :term:`S`\\ ``}``, the source directory. In the new terminal, "
"all the OpenEmbedded build-related environment variables are still "
"defined so you can use commands such as ``configure`` and ``make``. The "
"commands execute just as if the OpenEmbedded build system were executing "
"them. Consequently, working this way can be helpful when debugging a "
"build or preparing software to be used with the OpenEmbedded build "
"system."
msgstr ""

