#: ../../dev-manual/libraries.rst:100
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"For the most part, the :ref:`Multilib <ref-classes-multilib*>` class "
"extension works automatically to extend the package name from ``${PN}`` "
"to ``${MLPREFIX}${PN}``, where :term:`MLPREFIX` is the particular "
"multilib (e.g. \"lib32-\" or \"lib64-\"). Standard variables such as "
":term:`DEPENDS`, :term:`RDEPENDS`, :term:`RPROVIDES`, "
":term:`RRECOMMENDS`, :term:`PACKAGES`, and :term:`PACKAGES_DYNAMIC` are "
"automatically extended by the system. If you are extending any manual "
"code in the recipe, you can use the ``${MLPREFIX}`` variable to ensure "
"those names are extended correctly."
