#: ../../dev-manual/licenses.rst:4
msgid "Working With Licenses"
msgstr ""

#: ../../dev-manual/licenses.rst:6
msgid ""
"As mentioned in the \":ref:`overview-manual/development-"
"environment:licensing`\" section in the Yocto Project Overview and "
"Concepts Manual, open source projects are open to the public and they "
"consequently have different licensing structures in place. This section "
"describes the mechanism by which the :term:`OpenEmbedded Build System` "
"tracks changes to licensing text and covers how to maintain open source "
"license compliance during your project's lifecycle. The section also "
"describes how to enable commercially licensed recipes, which by default "
"are disabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../dev-manual/licenses.rst:17
msgid "Tracking License Changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../dev-manual/licenses.rst:19
msgid ""
"The license of an upstream project might change in the future. In order "
"to prevent these changes going unnoticed, the :term:`LIC_FILES_CHKSUM` "
"variable tracks changes to the license text. The checksums are validated "
"at the end of the configure step, and if the checksums do not match, the "
"build will fail."
msgstr ""

#: ../../dev-manual/licenses.rst:27
msgid "Specifying the ``LIC_FILES_CHKSUM`` Variable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../dev-manual/licenses.rst:29
msgid ""
"The :term:`LIC_FILES_CHKSUM` variable contains checksums of the license "
"text in the source code for the recipe. Here is an example of how to "
"specify :term:`LIC_FILES_CHKSUM`::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../dev-manual/licenses.rst:40
msgid ""
"When using \"beginline\" and \"endline\", realize that line numbering "
"begins with one and not zero. Also, the included lines are inclusive "
"(i.e. lines five through and including 29 in the previous example for "
"``licfile1.txt``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../dev-manual/licenses.rst:45
msgid ""
"When a license check fails, the selected license text is included as part"
" of the QA message. Using this output, you can determine the exact start "
"and finish for the needed license text."
msgstr ""

#: ../../dev-manual/licenses.rst:49
msgid ""
"The build system uses the :term:`S` variable as the default directory "
"when searching files listed in :term:`LIC_FILES_CHKSUM`. The previous "
"example employs the default directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../dev-manual/licenses.rst:54
msgid "Consider this next example::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../dev-manual/licenses.rst:60
