#: ../../dev-manual/qemu.rst:157
msgid "Switching Between Consoles"
msgstr ""

#: ../../dev-manual/qemu.rst:159
msgid ""
"When booting or running QEMU, you can switch between supported consoles "
"by using Ctrl+Alt+number. For example, Ctrl+Alt+3 switches you to the "
"serial console as long as that console is enabled. Being able to switch "
"consoles is helpful, for example, if the main QEMU console breaks for "
"some reason."
msgstr ""

#: ../../dev-manual/qemu.rst:167
msgid ""
"Usually, \"2\" gets you to the main console and \"3\" gets you to the "
"serial console."
msgstr ""

#: ../../dev-manual/qemu.rst:171
msgid "Removing the Splash Screen"
msgstr ""

#: ../../dev-manual/qemu.rst:173
msgid ""
"You can remove the splash screen when QEMU is booting by using Alt+left. "
"Removing the splash screen allows you to see what is happening in the "
"background."
msgstr ""

#: ../../dev-manual/qemu.rst:178
msgid "Disabling the Cursor Grab"
msgstr ""

#: ../../dev-manual/qemu.rst:180
msgid ""
"The default QEMU integration captures the cursor within the main window. "
"It does this since standard mouse devices only provide relative input and"
" not absolute coordinates. You then have to break out of the grab using "
"the \"Ctrl+Alt\" key combination. However, the Yocto Project's "
"integration of QEMU enables the wacom USB touch pad driver by default to "
"allow input of absolute coordinates. This default means that the mouse "
"can enter and leave the main window without the grab taking effect "
"leading to a better user experience."
msgstr ""

#: ../../dev-manual/qemu.rst:190
msgid "Running Under a Network File System (NFS) Server"
msgstr ""

#: ../../dev-manual/qemu.rst:192
msgid ""
"One method for running QEMU is to run it on an NFS server. This is useful"
" when you need to access the same file system from both the build and the"
" emulated system at the same time. It is also worth noting that the "
"system does not need root privileges to run. It uses a user space NFS "
"server to avoid that. Follow these steps to set up for running QEMU using"
" an NFS server."
msgstr ""

