#: ../../dev-manual/qemu.rst:365
msgid "``runqemu`` Command-Line Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../dev-manual/qemu.rst:367
msgid ""
"Here is a description of ``runqemu`` options you can provide on the "
"command line:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../dev-manual/qemu.rst:372
msgid ""
"If you do provide some \"illegal\" option combination or perhaps you do "
"not provide enough in the way of options, ``runqemu`` provides "
"appropriate error messaging to help you correct the problem."
msgstr ""

#: ../../dev-manual/qemu.rst:376
msgid ""
"`QEMUARCH`: The QEMU machine architecture, which must be \"qemuarm\", "
"\"qemuarm64\", \"qemumips\", \"qemumips64\", \"qemuppc\", \"qemux86\", or"
" \"qemux86-64\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../dev-manual/qemu.rst:380
msgid ""
"`VM`: The virtual machine image, which must be a ``.wic.vmdk`` file. Use "
"this option when you want to boot a ``.wic.vmdk`` image."
msgstr ""

#: ../../dev-manual/qemu.rst:383
msgid ""
"`ROOTFS`: A root filesystem that has one of the following filetype "
"extensions: \"ext2\", \"ext3\", \"ext4\", \"jffs2\", \"nfs\", or "
"\"btrfs\". If the filename you provide for this option uses \"nfs\", it "
"must provide an explicit root filesystem path."
msgstr ""

#: ../../dev-manual/qemu.rst:388
msgid ""
"`KERNEL`: A kernel image, which is a ``.bin`` file. When you provide a "
"``.bin`` file, ``runqemu`` detects it and assumes the file is a kernel "
"image."
msgstr ""

#: ../../dev-manual/qemu.rst:392
msgid ""
"`MACHINE`: The architecture of the QEMU machine, which must be one of the"
" following: \"qemux86\", \"qemux86-64\", \"qemuarm\", \"qemuarm64\", "
"\"qemumips\", \"qemumips64\", or \"qemuppc\". The MACHINE and QEMUARCH "
"options are basically identical. If you do not provide a MACHINE option, "
"``runqemu`` tries to determine it based on other options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../dev-manual/qemu.rst:398
msgid ""
"``ramfs``: Indicates you are booting an :term:`Initramfs` image, which "
"means the ``FSTYPE`` is ``cpio.gz``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../dev-manual/qemu.rst:401
msgid ""
"``iso``: Indicates you are booting an ISO image, which means the "
"``FSTYPE`` is ``.iso``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../dev-manual/qemu.rst:404
msgid ""
"``nographic``: Disables the video console, which sets the console to "
"\"ttys0\". This option is useful when you have logged into a server and "
"you do not want to disable forwarding from the X Window System (X11) to "
"your workstation or laptop."
msgstr ""

#: ../../dev-manual/qemu.rst:409
msgid "``serial``: Enables a serial console on ``/dev/ttyS0``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../dev-manual/qemu.rst:411
msgid ""
"``biosdir``: Establishes a custom directory for BIOS, VGA BIOS and "
"keymaps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../dev-manual/qemu.rst:414
msgid "``biosfilename``: Establishes a custom BIOS name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../dev-manual/qemu.rst:416
msgid ""
"``qemuparams=\\\"xyz\\\"``: Specifies custom QEMU parameters. Use this "
"option to pass options other than the simple \"kvm\" and \"serial\" "
"options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../dev-manual/qemu.rst:420
msgid ""
"``bootparams=\\\"xyz\\\"``: Specifies custom boot parameters for the "
"kernel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../dev-manual/qemu.rst:423
msgid ""
"``audio``: Enables audio in QEMU. The MACHINE option must be either "
"\"qemux86\" or \"qemux86-64\" in order for audio to be enabled. "
"Additionally, the ``snd_intel8x0`` or ``snd_ens1370`` driver must be "
"installed in linux guest."
msgstr ""

#: ../../dev-manual/qemu.rst:428
msgid ""
"``slirp``: Enables \"slirp\" networking, which is a different way of "
"networking that does not need root access but also is not as easy to use "
"or comprehensive as the default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../dev-manual/qemu.rst:432
msgid ""
"Using ``slirp`` by default will forward the guest machine's 22 and 23 TCP"
" ports to host machine's 2222 and 2323 ports (or the next free ports). "
"Specific forwarding rules can be configured by setting ``QB_SLIRP_OPT`` "
"as environment variable or in ``qemuboot.conf`` in the :term:`Build "
"Directory` ``deploy/image`` directory. Examples::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../dev-manual/qemu.rst:443
msgid ""
"The first example forwards TCP port 80 from the emulated system to port "
"8080 (or the next free port) on the host system, allowing access to an "
"http server running in QEMU from ``http://<host ip>:8080/``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../dev-manual/qemu.rst:448
msgid ""
"The second example does the same, but also forwards TCP port 22 on the "
"guest system to 2222 (or the next free port) on the host system, allowing"
" ssh access to the emulated system using ``ssh -P 2222 <user>@<host "
"ip>``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../dev-manual/qemu.rst:453
msgid "Keep in mind that proper configuration of firewall software is required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../dev-manual/qemu.rst:455
msgid ""
"``kvm``: Enables KVM when running \"qemux86\" or \"qemux86-64\" QEMU "
"architectures. For KVM to work, all the following conditions must be met:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../dev-manual/qemu.rst:459
msgid "Your MACHINE must be either qemux86\" or \"qemux86-64\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../dev-manual/qemu.rst:461
msgid ""
"Your build host has to have the KVM modules installed, which are "
"``/dev/kvm``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../dev-manual/qemu.rst:464
msgid ""
"The build host ``/dev/kvm`` directory has to be both writable and "
"readable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../dev-manual/qemu.rst:467
msgid ""
"``kvm-vhost``: Enables KVM with VHOST support when running \"qemux86\" or"
" \"qemux86-64\" QEMU architectures. For KVM with VHOST to work, the "
"following conditions must be met:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../dev-manual/qemu.rst:471
msgid "``kvm`` option conditions defined above must be met."
msgstr ""

#: ../../dev-manual/qemu.rst:473
msgid ""
"Your build host has to have virtio net device, which are ``/dev/vhost-"
"net``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../dev-manual/qemu.rst:476
msgid ""
"The build host ``/dev/vhost-net`` directory has to be either readable or "
"writable and \"slirp-enabled\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../dev-manual/qemu.rst:479
msgid "``publicvnc``: Enables a VNC server open to all hosts."
msgstr ""

